52. FINAL PRINCIPLE

iRiel Devices are not designed to make the human dependent on the cloud.

They are designed to make personal intelligence physically available within the user's own computing environment.

The device should process locally when possible.

The system should minimize what leaves the device.

When external processing is necessary, it must be authorized, minimized, protected and transparent.

The device may change.

The AI provider may change.

The infrastructure may change.

The cloud may change.

The user's identity remains.

The human remains in control.


53. CANONICAL DEFINITION

iRiel Devices are intelligent computing devices designed to host, process, preserve and manage components of a person's Personal Intelligence Environment, prioritizing local processing, local data, privacy, accessibility, intelligent storage and human control while remaining independent from any specific AI provider, cloud infrastructure or device ecosystem.


